## Context: the defect this bead repairs
`TestMergeDriverWithLockedConfig_E2E/handles_read-only_git_config_file` failed
before this item started. Cause, reproduced independently on git 2.43.0: `git
config` writes through a lock file plus rename inside `.git/`, so a mode-0444
`.git/config` is still rewritten while the `.git/` DIRECTORY stays writable. The
test chmodded the file but not the directory, so its premise was false and
`MergeDriver` correctly returned nil. The product code was right; the test was
wrong.

## Look hardest at
- Does the repaired test now actually prevent the write, rather than weakening
  the assertion or narrowing the case until it passes? A test that no longer
  proves `MergeDriver` reports a config-write failure is worse than the broken
  one.
- Does it still assert the error mentions "failed to update git merge driver
  config"?
- Cleanup: an unwritable directory left behind breaks `t.TempDir` teardown and
  every later run. Verify permissions are restored on every exit path,
  including the failure path.
- Is the test skipped, deleted, or added to `.test-skip` anywhere? Any of those
  is a high finding — the bead forbids all three.
- Does it remain correct for a root user and on macOS (the existing skips at
  the top of the test)?

